My archeologist hasn't been doing bad so far in this game:

I got a /oPolymorph early on (sokoban?), and turned Puppy in to Purple
Worm. Sweeeeeet.  One mostly empty minetown later, I've got some
protection, but no shopkeeper I can price-id ID with...  So I'm kind of
bummed by that difficulty, but not too terribly much.  I figure I'll find
some way around it.  I also got a magic lamp out of the deal, which was
great - most of the mines were dark.

Sokoban gave me a "oReflection, so I was hurting for a bag of holding -
especially as I was trucking around with +1 Banded mail, which while nice,
weighs a lot.  But I was able to handle being burdened, what with the
Purple Worm - I just stayed away from all these 'c's that kept showing
up...  My second dog turned into a brown pudding, and they *will* attack
'c's, and if they get hit, they  multiply :)  Maybe I should have taken up
farming...  But I don't have a magic whistle, so I left my 3 Christmas
puddings in the mines...

I figured if I was going to go polymorphing, I might as well empty the
tool shed...and sure enough, I got a bag of holding on my 3rd or 4th zap -
so I'm *quite* pleased!  I may go back to try for the magic whistle.  I
sacrificed a chickatrice corpse (checked gloves twice) and got Snickersee.
 Ok, that's cool.  I really wanted to try quisennart with double silver
 saber, but I can live with Snickersee.

Back in the main dungeon, though, things get even better!  I find an
antique weapons outlet, and the owner is being obnoxious about my pickaxe.
 Feeling my honor a bit sullied, I order Puppy in to settle matters with
 the guy:

Puppy bites Echourgnac.  Puppy swallows Echourgnac.  "Burrrrp!" 
Echourgnac is killed!

As I'm going through the shop, I stumble across Grayswandir!  WOOT!  Now,
pity that the guard captain in minetown only had a long swor....oh, MY - a
silver saber in the shop, too!

AC is -7 now with Dwarven Mithril, not burdened, have reflection, and can
go Chop-chop-chop!  This is gonna be fun :-)

